kind: vulnerability
title: "Microsoft May 2026 Patch Tuesday: Windows Netlogon RCE CVE-2026-41089 (exploitation reported by CCB, not confirmed by Microsoft) and three further critical flaws"
headline: "Netlogon flaw CVE-2026-41089 on domain controllers: Belgium's CCB reports exploitation, Microsoft says it has no evidence"
summary: "Microsoft's May 2026 updates fixed CVE-2026-41089, an unauthenticated stack-based buffer overflow in Windows Netlogon on domain controllers (CVSS 9.8), alongside critical flaws in the Windows DNS Client (CVE-2026-41096), the Microsoft SSO Plugin for Jira and Confluence (CVE-2026-41103) and Dynamics 365 on-premises (CVE-2026-42898). Belgium's CCB said on 2026-05-29 that the Netlogon flaw is exploited in the wild and CERT-EU relayed that on 2026-06-10, but Microsoft told reporters it has no evidence of exploitation, its advisory does not mark it exploited and CISA has not listed it."
event_date: 2026-05-12
priority: notable
immediate_action: null
tags:
  - vulnerabilities
  - rce
  - pre-auth
  - patch-available
regions:
  - global
  - europe
sectors: []
entities: []
techniques: [T1210, T1499.004]
affected_products: ["Microsoft Windows Server", "Microsoft Dynamics 365", "Microsoft SSO Plugin for Jira and Confluence"]
